      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.44,
      "end": 1.94,
      "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.79,
      "end": 16.03,
      "text": "That's called legginess, and it's really common. They're stretching towards the light because they aren't getting enough."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.52,
      "end": 27.43,
      "text": "Even a bright window is dim compared to outside in early spring. Turning the tray every day helps, and a cheap grow light helps a lot more."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 34.455,
      "end": 41.585,
      "text": "Tomatoes are great at this, you can save them. When you pot them on, bury the stem right up to the first leaves. It'll grow roots all along it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 47.235,
      "end": 52.825,
      "text": "Really. It's one of the few plants that loves it. You'll end up with sturdier plants than if they'd never flopped."
    }
